  "title": "Nomadic Life",
  "description": "Gyani Maiya Sen-Kusunda (1937–2020), a community elder from Kulmor, Dang district, Nepal, talks with Uday Raj Aaley in Kusunda about her nomadic life in the forest. The community calls the language Gejmehac Gipan, the \"forest king's language\". Her community later left nomadic life and settled in villages around the district. Subhashish Panigrahi recorded it in 2018 for his 2019 documentary Gyani Maiya. It was edited from footage unused or little used in the film and published under the Gejmehac Gipan project in 2024. Kusunda and Nepali subtitles are by Aaley, and the English subtitles are by Panigrahi with Aaley's help.",
